  "body": "For possible values of the fontStretch attribute, [the HTML spec](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#dom-context-2d-fontstretch) currently lists only the CSS `font-stretch` keywords ranging from `ultra-condensed` to `ultra-expanded`.\r\n\r\nHowever, [the CSS `font-stretch` property](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts-4/#font-stretch-prop) also accepts percentage values, which may map to a variable-font \"width\" axis for finer control. I think the canvas attribute should match this.\r\n\r\n(Note that there's also [a separate pre-existing issue](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/8103) concerning `fontStretch`, which is the question of how it interacts with the `font` attribute, given that it is possible for a stretch value -- though not a percentage -- to be included in the font shorthand, potentially conflicting with the value of the separate attribute.)",
